460→# Alternative: Direct Change Application
461→
462→Besides the sync protocol, you can also apply changes directly:
463→
464→```csharp
465→// Get all changes from one document
466→var changes = doc1.GetChanges(new string[0]);
467→
468→// Apply them to another document
469→doc2.ApplyChanges(changes);
470→```
471→
472→This approach works but is less efficient. It sends all changes, not just the differences.
473→
474→The sync protocol is preferred for:
475→- Real-time collaboration
476→- Frequent updates
477→- Limited bandwidth
478→- Long-running connections
479→
480→Direct change application works for:
481→- One-time merges
482→- Batch updates
483→- Simple scenarios
484→
485→# Handling Disconnections
486→
487→The sync protocol handles disconnections gracefully:
488→
489→```csharp
490→using var alice = AutomergeDocument.Create();
491→using var bob = AutomergeDocument.Create();
492→using var aliceSync = alice.CreateSyncState();
493→using var bobSync = bob.CreateSyncState();
494→
495→// Initial sync
496→SyncDocuments(alice, bob, aliceSync, bobSync);
497→
498→// Alice makes changes while disconnected
499→var aliceRoot = alice.RootId;
500→alice.PutString(aliceRoot, "field1", "value1");
501→alice.Commit("Offline change 1");
502→alice.PutString(aliceRoot, "field2", "value2");
503→alice.Commit("Offline change 2");
504→
505→// Bob makes changes while disconnected
506→var bobRoot = bob.RootId;
507→bob.PutString(bobRoot, "field3", "value3");
508→bob.Commit("Offline change 3");
509→
510→// Reconnect and sync
511→SyncDocuments(alice, bob, aliceSync, bobSync);
512→
513→// Both documents now have all six fields
514→```
515→
516→The sync state tracks what was sent before the disconnection. On reconnection, only new changes transfer.
517→
518→# Best Practices
519→
520→## One Sync State Per Peer
521→
522→Create a separate sync state for each peer you sync with:
523→
524→```csharp
525→// Good: Separate states
526→var syncToBob = alice.CreateSyncState();
527→var syncToCarol = alice.CreateSyncState();
528→
529→// Wrong: Reusing sync state for different peers
530→var sync = alice.CreateSyncState(); // Don't use with multiple peers
531→```
532→
533→## Persist Sync State for Long-Running Applications
534→
535→Save sync state between sessions:
536→
537→```csharp
538→// On shutdown
539→var encoded = syncState.Encode();
540→await File.WriteAllBytesAsync("sync-state.bin", encoded);
541→
542→// On startup
543→var bytes = await File.ReadAllBytesAsync("sync-state.bin");
544→using var syncState = AutomergeSyncState.Decode(bytes);
545→```
546→
547→## Limit Sync Rounds
548→
549→Always set a maximum number of rounds to prevent infinite loops:
550→
551→```csharp
552→void SyncDocuments(
553→    AutomergeDocument doc1,
554→    AutomergeDocument doc2,
555→    AutomergeSyncState state1,
556→    AutomergeSyncState state2,
557→    int maxRounds = 10) // Limit rounds
558→{
559→    for (int i = 0; i < maxRounds; i++)
560→    {
561→        // Sync logic...
562→    }
563→}
564→```
565→
566→## Handle Sync Errors
567→
568→Wrap sync operations in try-catch:
569→
570→```csharp
571→try
572→{
573→    doc.ReceiveSyncMessage(syncState, message);
574→}
575→catch (AutomergeException ex)
576→{
577→    Console.WriteLine($"Sync error: {ex.Message}");
578→    // Possibly reset sync state and retry
579→    syncState.Reset();
580→}
581→```
582→
583→## Dispose Sync States
584→
585→Always dispose sync states when done:
586→
587→```csharp
588→using var syncState = doc.CreateSyncState();
589→// Use sync state
590→// Automatic disposal happens here
591→```
