  8→/// <remarks>
  9→/// KNOWN ISSUE: These tests suffer from a critical bug in the automerge Rust FFI library (v0.7.0).
 10→/// When running tests as a group, the second test crashes with:
 11→///   - "AUTOMERGE :: unused actor found when none expected"
 12→///   - "assertion failed: !panic" at automerge-0.7.0/src/automerge.rs:300:13
 13→///   - Crash in automerge_doc_sync_generate_message
 14→///
 15→/// The tests MUST run serially (enforced via xUnit collection) and even with 8-second delays
 16→/// between tests, the issue persists. This indicates a fundamental bug in either:
 17→///   1. The automerge Rust library's internal state management
 18→///   2. The C# FFI wrapper's interaction with the Rust library
 19→///   3. Thread safety violations at the FFI boundary
 20→///
 21→/// Individual tests pass reliably. The crash only occurs when running multiple tests sequentially.
 22→/// See OpenSpec proposal for investigation and fix.
